      "id": "s2",
      "type": "sharedSection",
      "props": {
        "sectionId": "split-band",
        "values": {
          "eyebrow": "",
          "heading": "",
          "body": "Bob was well known in and around the rural Southwest Wisconsin community, having lived in the region his entire 35 years. A decade earlier, he drove his own milk route, collecting Grade B milk from the region’s abundant dairy farms for delivery to Brewery Hill Cheese factory. He used to be a cheese-maker, before becoming a long-distance trucker. He later co-owned Mc-Mor-Han Trucking Company, which had been hauling livestock and fertilizer for eight years, and had been selling GMC pick-up trucks since 1958.\n\nMore than 60 years after Shullsburg, the McCoy Group has grown into a corporation with five subsidiaries that reaches across North America.\n\nCurrently, the McCoy Group consists of Truck Country/Stoops Freightliner-Western Star, Foodliner, Quest Liner, Foodliner Mexico/Quest Liner Mexico and McCoy Construction & Forestry, employing more than 3,600 people.",
          "image": {
            "src": "https://www.truckcountry.com/efs/wp/domains/www.truckcountry.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/GMC-red-Bob1-848x585-1.webp",
